  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNFIL)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) was originally created with the adoption of Security Council Resolution 425 and 426 on 19 March 1978, to confirm Israeli withdrawal from Lebanon which Israel had invaded five days prior, restore international peace and security, and help the Government of Lebanon restore its effective authority in the area. Following the 2006 Lebanon War, the United Nations Security Council enhanced UNIFIL and decided that in addition to the original mandate, it would monitor the cessation of hostilities; accompany and support the Lebanese Armed Forces as they deploy throughout the south of Lebanon; and extend its assistance to help ensure humanitarian access to civilian populations and the voluntary and safe return of displaced persons. Funding under this activity represents Australia&apos;s assessed contribution to the operation.</narrative>
  </description>
